<div style="width: 100%; background-color: #1a5276; color: white; text-align: center; padding: 15px 0; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 20px 0 10px 0; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 11th Grade (CEFR: B1.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Intelligent Robots</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> What is Artificial Intelligence?</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Develop instructions for everyday tasks. Interactive: Revise classmates' essays on general topics.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can develop step-by-step instructions for using AI tools in everyday life, using simple language for clarity (e.g., "Open the app and select a task to get suggestions from the AI assistant.")
            Can edit and revise essays on AI, ensuring clarity in descriptions of technology (e.g., "Explain how AI assists in daily tasks like organizing schedules.")
            Can provide feedback on classmates' writing about AI, suggesting examples to clarify abstract ideas (e.g., "Add examples of AI used in customer service.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 40%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 45%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 15%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by displaying images of various AI tools (e.g., a smart assistant, an AI-powered translation app, a robotic vacuum cleaner). Students are asked to quickly jot down one sentence predicting what each tool will do in the future. Example prompt: "If AI continues to evolve, these robots might..." This activates prior knowledge and introduces the writing focus.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to write clear, simple instructions using conditional forms and future simple. For instance, the teacher writes "How to use an AI music generator" on the board and drafts the first two steps: "1. Open the AI music app. 2. If you want a specific style, select a genre. The AI will then create a song for you." The teacher highlights the use of the conditional and future simple, as well as the need for concise language. The teacher also models the pronunciation of words like "robot" /ɑː/ and "innovative" /ɪn.əˈveɪ.tɪv/ while speaking.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What type of sentences did I use to give advice or possibilities?" (Expected answer: Conditionals, e.g., "If you want...")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What tense tells us what the AI is going to do?" (Expected answer: Future simple, e.g., "will create...")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Are these instructions clear for someone who has never used this tool?" (Expected answer: Yes/No, and why).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Intelligent Robots".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher distributes a short written text, perhaps a "User Manual Excerpt for a Home Assistant Robot" (genre: instructions/technical description). The text describes the basic functionality of a smart robot designed to assist with household tasks. It clearly demonstrates step-by-step instructions and descriptions of features using conditional forms, future simple, and passive voice. For example: "If the robot encounters an obstacle, it will automatically reroute. AI systems are programmed to learn from new environments." The text integrates vocabulary like <i>functionality, systems, improve, data, personalize</i>.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Express ideas and information in writing using appropriate structures for different communicative purposes, such as giving instructions or describing functionality.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the text and identify the main purpose of the robot by circling the key action verbs.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students complete True/False statements about the robot's capabilities and its programming. Example: "AI systems are programmed to forget old data." (False)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students underline all sentences containing conditional forms, future simple, or passive voice, then identify specific vocabulary words (e.g., <i>advance, evolve, enhance, responsible, technological</i>).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Developing written instructions and descriptions using conditional forms (e.g., "If AI continues to evolve..."), future simple (e.g., "AI will create new opportunities."), passive voice (e.g., "AI systems are programmed..."). Integrating vocabulary: <i>artificial intelligence, robots, technology, society, opportunities, challenges, job markets, employment, algorithms, data, software, functionality, systems, updates, improve, advance, evolve, revolutionize, adapt, create, enhance, personalize, integrate, prepare, learn, apply, intelligent, responsible, complex, societal, drastic, significant, evolving, future, revolutionary, personalized, controlled, passive, functional, enhanced, innovative, technological.</i></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Sentence Transformation):</b> Students work individually to rewrite sentences, applying specific grammatical structures.
                        <br>a. Change active voice to passive voice: "Engineers program AI systems." → "AI systems <i>are programmed</i> by engineers."
                        <br>b. Combine sentences using conditionals: "AI learns from data. It improves its performance." → "If AI <i>learns</i> from data, it <i>will improve</i> its performance."
                        <br>c. Complete sentences with future simple verbs and target vocabulary: "Future AI (___) (create) new (___) in the (___) (market)." (Expected: "Future AI <i>will create</i> new <i>opportunities</i> in the <i>job market</i>.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Guided Instruction Writing):</b> The teacher provides sentence starters or key phrases for describing a simple AI task. Students must complete them to form coherent instructions, focusing on sequence and clarity. Example: "First, (verb) the (noun)... If you (verb) (noun), the AI (future simple verb)... The data (passive voice verb) to (verb)..."
                        <br>This encourages the use of transition words and precise vocabulary related to AI.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Check & Peer Feedback:</b> Students exchange their written instruction sentences from activity 2 with a partner. Partners check for:
                        <br>a. Correct use of conditional forms, future simple, and passive voice.
                        <br>b. Appropriate integration of at least three new vocabulary words related to AI (e.g., <i>algorithms, functionality, enhance</i>).
                        <br>c. Clarity and logical flow of the instructions.
                        <br>They provide written feedback using polite language (sociolinguistic: "How might you clarify this step?" or "I predict this instruction could be more effective if...").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Intelligent Robots".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Written Product & Peer Revision.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Activity: "AI Tool User Manual Entry"</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in pairs. Each pair imagines they are technical writers creating a short user manual entry for a new, simple AI tool or robot that helps with an everyday task. They choose one task (e.g., an AI study assistant, a smart calendar organizer, a robotic pet feeder, a personalized learning software). Their task is to write:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A brief description of the AI tool, using at least two passive voice sentences (e.g., "This innovative software is designed to personalize learning experiences.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Step-by-step instructions (4-5 steps) on how to use the tool effectively, incorporating conditional forms (e.g., "If you want to organize your schedule, open the app first.") and future simple (e.g., "The AI will predict your busiest times.").</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Once completed, pairs swap their manual entries with another pair. They then act as "editors" and provide constructive feedback on their classmates' writing, focusing on:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of instructions (Are the steps easy to follow?).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accuracy of grammar (conditionals, future simple, passive voice).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (<i>algorithms, functionality, enhance, update, improve</i>).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Suggesting examples to clarify abstract ideas (e.g., "Could you add an example of how the AI 'personalizes' the experience?").</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students rewrite their entries based on the feedback. The teacher monitors, provides support, and encourages thoughtful discussion about AI's impact (sociolinguistic: "How might this AI tool change daily jobs?").</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist and peer assessment rubric.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their final, revised "AI Tool User Manual Entry." The teacher collects these for review and provides feedback on clarity, grammar, and vocabulary usage.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and logical sequence of instructions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct and appropriate use of conditional forms.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of future simple for predictions/outcomes.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective use of passive voice in descriptions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Integration of at least 5 target vocabulary words.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Overall coherence, grammar, and spelling.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a short reflection:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most challenging part of writing clear instructions about AI, and how did I overcome it?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How confident do I feel in using conditional forms and passive voice in my writing now?" (Scale of 1-5).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What specific feedback from my classmates helped me improve my writing the most, and why?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How will developing step-by-step instructions for AI tools benefit me in the future, perhaps in my career?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What worked well in helping students integrate conditional forms, future simple, and passive voice into their writing?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for students who struggled with clarity or grammar accuracy in their instructions?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did students engage effectively in the peer revision process, and were their feedback suggestions helpful?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration), students will summarize their user manual entries and present key information about their AI tools to the class. They will explain how AI functions and its societal implications, drawing on their developed instructions and descriptions.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>